 12, the record for Berrien County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids August to September came in under 90% of normal in 34 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle saw January to February at 66% of normal and August to September at 71%. So far in 2026 the middle has March to April at 181% of normal. Grid 26276 had its driest year in 1953 at 70% of normal.</p>"}
